# ComposeBus Kernel — bare-instantiable, locality-recursive, multi-attach; PLACEMENT UNRATIFIED [SPEC:CXC-COMPOSEBUS-KERNEL]

> ComposeBus is a kernel, not an MQTT client: a bare `ComposeBus()` instantiates with zero arguments and zero paho import, and MQTT is one registry-factory connector among several (CAN, UART, LoRa, segment-bridge) rather than a hardcoded dependency. Standup is a fixed three-step sequence — bare bus, attach declared connectors (MULTI-ATTACH), load plugins respecting their `requires:` floor. The same kernel spec instantiates recursively at every scale: an internal bus inside a mothercard is the SAME kernel at an inner locality, and a peripheral is a plugin of whichever kernel is local to it. A connector's job is bounded tightly — forward by scope, encode for the wire, never transform — so the kernel cannot become a hidden mediator.

---

## 1. The kernel is transport-agnostic and bare-instantiable

### [CXC-CBK-PLACEMENT] Placement is UNRATIFIED, and filename 84 was verified unused

- placement-status: UNRATIFIED. Written into `corpora/platform-specs/` because its nearest relatives (61, 62, 73, 79, 80, 81, 83) already sit there, several of them flagged `[PLACEMENT UNRATIFIED]` themselves — convention, not a ruling.
- filename-number-check: 84 was verified unused across `corpora/platform-specs/` before this file was written (highest prior number in sequence was 83; 99 is a reserved conventions-document number).
- provenance: architect-synthesis
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-COMPOSEBUS-KERNEL]
- see-also: [CXC-VISION-PLACEMENT]

### [CXC-CBK-MQTT-INDEPENDENT] The kernel is MQTT-independent — bare instantiation is the default, not a mode

- claim: A zero-argument `ComposeBus()` is the default and complete kernel. No `paho` import exists in the kernel itself. MQTT is ONE registry-factory connector, structurally equal to CAN and UART — the same status `transport_registry.py` already gives MQTT/CAN/UART/synthetic/replay at the Python transport-layer, generalized to the connector layer.
- measured: a sweep verdict recorded CLEAN against this claim in-session — zero-arg bare bus is the default, no paho in kernel, MQTT is one registry factory equal to CAN/UART.
- consolidates: today's fragmented per-service self-connect — `print_services` raw-paho, and two HTTP services each standing up their own client — collapses into one kernel with declared connectors, rather than N services each re-deriving a connection.
- status: proposed
- provenance: architect-synthesis
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-COMPOSEBUS-KERNEL]
- see-also: [CXC-CBK-STANDUP], [CXC-SOB-THESIS]

