## 5. Primary render surface — DECIDED

### [DD-CBK-PRIMARY-RENDER-SURFACE] A node's primary display IS a wrapped participant like every peripheral — the carve-out is killed

- question: is the node's main display a wrapped participant exactly like every other peripheral ([CXC-CBK-PERIPHERAL-PLUGIN-MODEL]), or is it the one carve-out — a non-wrapped, directly-owned realization?
- decision: DECIDED — participant. David ruled "kill the carve-out" (line 23408): the primary render surface IS a wrapped participant — the node's principal subscribe+publish plugin — held to [CXC-CBK-PERIPHERAL-PLUGIN-MODEL] with NO exception. There is no special-cased, non-wrapped display tier.
- rationale: [CXC-CBK-PERIPHERAL-PLUGIN-MODEL] generalizes cleanly to the primary display when it is wrapped like any other peripheral; a carve-out is an asymmetry the model does not otherwise need. David's ruling follows the model's own grain, so [CXC-CBK-PERIPHERAL-PLUGIN-MODEL] needs no exception clause — the primary display is simply one more instance of it.
- rejected-alternative: carve-out — keeping the primary display as the one non-wrapped, directly-owned realization. Ruled OUT by David at line 23408.
- change: the primary-render-surface fork is RESOLVED toward participant — David ruled "kill the carve-out" (line 23408) after the architect ran the stress-test straw man. The earlier WIP capture had recorded it "PENDING (this turn)"; that pending state is now closed.
- context_for_change:
  prior_state: the WIP capture this document was first authored from recorded the fork as "PENDING (this turn)" with a stated leaning toward participant, and an earlier draft carried a self-contradictory provenance-caveat (a david-ruling tag on a node whose body said "not yet decided").
  reasoning: after the architect ran the stress-test straw man, David explicitly ruled "kill the carve-out" (line 23408) — the primary display is a wrapped participant like every peripheral, no special case.
  rejected_alternative: leave the primary render surface as a permanent non-wrapped exception.
  invalidating_assumption: if the primary display is later found to have a genuine structural need the peripheral-plugin model cannot express (e.g. a boot-time render path that must exist before any plugin loader runs), the carve-out reopens and this decision is revisited.
  implication: [CXC-CBK-PERIPHERAL-PLUGIN-MODEL] needs NO amendment and NO exception clause — the primary display is one more instance of it.
- invalidating_assumption: if the primary display is later found to have a genuine structural need the peripheral-plugin model cannot express (e.g. a boot-time render path that must exist before any plugin loader runs), the carve-out reopens and this decision is revisited. (Restated as a top-level property so the DD-family schema can find it directly; the fuller change record lives in `context_for_change` above.)
- status: decided
- status-detail: decided 2026-08-23 — David ruled "kill the carve-out" (line 23408). The prior raised/pending state is closed. The DD- id is retained (this corpus uses DD- for both open and ruled design decisions, e.g. [DD-DRI-BRACKET-KEY-VERDICT]), so no re-id is needed and no dangle is created.
- provenance: david-ruling — David's explicit ruling at line 23408: "In any event, I agree - kill the carve-out."
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-COMPOSEBUS-KERNEL]
- see-also: [CXC-CBK-PERIPHERAL-PLUGIN-MODEL]
- alternatives: participant (CHOSEN, David's ruling): wrap the primary display exactly like any other peripheral, per [CXC-CBK-PERIPHERAL-PLUGIN-MODEL]. carve-out (REJECTED, line 23408): keep the primary display as the one non-wrapped, directly-owned realization.

