### [CXC-CBK-PKG-EVIDENCE] POST-integration evidence slots — every one EMPTY until the builder fills it with a measured value

- rule: per [DX-SPEC-CARRIES-ITS-EVIDENCE], an unfilled slot carries the literal `EMPTY`, never absence. `EMPTY` means this packaging has never been built and verified; the builder replaces each value with the raw measured output and the date.
- baseline-test-counts-before: At 07348ff (run twice, scratch venv mirroring system site-packages, composeio not installed): python/tests "3 failed, 4139 passed, 24 skipped, 9 xfailed" (twice); repo-root tests/ "3 failed, 593 passed, 47 skipped"; compose_projects/intelligence "184 passed". The 3 python failures predate this change (test_m31_composer_chrome_golden; test_converted_source_blocks_and_then_stops[lts_engine_status] and [daemon_watch]). Logs and junit: (a local path, not published) (before2-*). Builder run 2026-11-25; independently compared by composeplatform-qa.
- after-test-counts: At 6a14673, with the new packaging test file excluded: python/tests "3 failed, 4139 passed, 24 skipped, 9 xfailed", n=4175, per-test-id status-changed [] (only-before [], only-after []); root tests/ n=643 status-changed []; intelligence n=184 status-changed []. New tests: test_composebus_packaging.py 45 passed; python/composebus/tests 120 passed. QA re-verdict PASS_WITH_NOTES (its own junit diff: zero changed tests; spot runs of 172 python + 226 root tests with no status differences). junit: cbk/after2-*.
- closure-check-output: Builder's closure test against the installed copy: "files_scanned: 20 / import_statements_classified: 106 / nested_imports: 13 / distinct_roots: __future__ abc collections composebus dataclasses enum json logging pydantic re sys threading time typing weakref / violations: 0 / closure_exit=0". Negative control: a planted lazy `from composeio.transforms import TransformChain` in a scratch copy was caught (1 violation). QA's independent AST walk (every depth, plus dynamic-import calls): 20 files, 0 violations; it catches injected composeio.peer and yaml imports, and fails on an empty directory.
- identity-check-output: python/tests/test_composebus_packaging.py at 6a14673: 45 passed. It covers the 13 moved modules and 5 plugin submodules (`composeio.X is composebus.X`), composeio.plugins as a real package, the non-moving plugins importable from composeio only, class identity, a monkeypatch round-trip, no extra deletions, the real __spec__ kept, and reload re-executing through both names. QA independently checked 13+5 modules from five entrypoint styles (cd python; PYTHONPATH=python; installed composebus with and without the checkout; the editable pair): no identity failures and no file loaded twice.
- contents-check-output: Installed copy: "files_found: 20 (__init__ bus bus_clock bus_envelope freshness module namespace plugin plugins/__init__ plugins/discovery plugins/liveness plugins/log plugins/state_manager plugins/time selector state_engine transforms transport transport_contract transport_local) / missing: [] / unexpected: [] / RESULT: MATCH". `git diff --diff-filter=D 07348ff..` under python/composeio lists exactly the 18 moved files. Wheel composebus-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl: 25 files, including dist-info/licenses/LICENSE (1070 bytes, identical to the public repo LICENSE); METADATA "License: MIT", "Requires-Dist: pydantic>=2.0". The composeio wheel drops from 353 to 335 files (exactly the 18) and gains "Requires-Dist: composebus==0.1.0".
- standalone-venv-subset-result: Fresh venv holding only composebus 0.1.0 + pydantic + pytest (pip list: annotated-types, composebus, iniconfig, packaging, pip, pluggy, pydantic, pydantic_core, Pygments, pytest, typing_extensions, typing-inspection), tests run from outside the checkout with PYTHONPATH unset: "120 passed", subset_exit=0, at both 424f58e and 6a14673. QA reproduced this in its own fresh composebus[test] venv installed from the pin: 120 passed. Consumer smoke from the pin: a bare ComposeIOBus() publish/get returns 42, and add_binding with a scale transform returns 50.0.
- standalone-venv-subset-test-list: Selected by an AST scan for test files whose only non-stdlib imports are moved modules, pytest or pydantic (test_bus_storage_device_baseline.py excluded, because it loads services/bus_storage by path): test_bus 25, test_bus_clock 17, test_bus_concurrent_publish 3, test_bus_scope_auto_resolve_union 9, test_compound_bindings 13, test_liveness_d1_d2_bringup 2, test_modal_priority 5, test_selector 9, test_state_engines 19, test_transforms 15, plus new test_closure 1 and test_contents 2. Per test-import-rule, every changed line in the copies is an import line rewritten composeio->composebus; QA confirmed this for all 10 copies. The conftest fixtures (bus, local_transport) are copied verbatim apart from their imports.
- standalone-venv-negative-control-result: In the same fresh venv and directory: `python -c "import composeio"` gives "ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'composeio'", negative_control_exit=1. QA reproduced this in both of its venvs (the standalone one and the pin-install one).
- leak-hygiene-grep-output: Builder, every file of the exported python/composebus/: grep for *.local hostnames, other internal hostnames, RFC1918 IPs, /Users/ and /home/ paths, and zero ?biometric|haven. All five classes gave grep_exit=1 (no hits). QA, 36 tracked files: no hits; the only `.local` matches are Scope.LOCAL and Authority.LOCAL; the owner's name appears in LICENSE and docstrings, which HoP's ruling of 2026-11-25 permits.
- tag-annotated-check: `git cat-file -t composebus-v0.1.0` prints "tag", with no ambiguity warning now that the branch is named build/composebus-v0.1.0. Both pin forms (@composebus-v0.1.0 and @refs/tags/composebus-v0.1.0) installed commit_id 6a14673 (QA).
- tag-not-on-remote-check: Before publication: `git ls-remote --tags origin composebus-v0.1.0` and `--heads` for both branch names printed nothing (exit 0), from both the builder and QA. Publication to the public repo happens afterwards under DEC-HOP-STANDING-PUSH-AUTHORITY-COMPOSEIO-2026-11-25 and is recorded under CXC-CBK-PKG-RELEASE.
